(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/main.asl#" :text "JavaScript backend entry: compileEntry! links an entry module with asl-ir/link and emits one self-contained ES module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/main.asl#compileEntry!" :text "Links the program at entryPath (prelude included) and returns the ES module text, or the link diagnostics, or ERR_CAPABILITY_ABSENT naming each host builtin the js runtime does not provide.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/emit.asl#" :text "SsaModule to JavaScript: one function per SSA function, its blocks as cases of a switch inside a loop, block parameters assigned on each edge; a self call whose result is returned (directly or through join blocks that only forward it) becomes a jump to the entry block, so the prelude's recursive loops run in constant stack. box and unbox are identities: Int is BigInt, Float is number, Bool is boolean.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/emit.asl#emitJsModule" :text "The module text: the runtime, the string pool, every function, and an export per function of the entry module under its ASL name (export { f as \"name?\" }), plus setOutput and AslTrap.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/runtime.asl#" :text "The JavaScript runtime as text: values (Variant, Rec, Cons lists with null as the empty list, Kw, Sym, UNIT), str/print formatting identical to the host (records as {:k v}, floats as the shortest round-trip digits laid out like python repr), int64 overflow and floor division traps, UTF-8 byte semantics for strings with BStr holding byte strings that are not valid UTF-8, and the builtin, entry and prim tables. Clocks are provided (nowNs from Date.now, monotonicNs from performance.now); files, processes and the environment are not.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/tests/emitJsTest.asl#" :text "Differential suite: every fixture is compiled to js and run under node, and its stdout, exit code and trap code must equal asl-host run of the same file; a program that reads a file must fail to compile with ERR_CAPABILITY_ABSENT.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/dts.asl#" :text "TypeScript declarations for an entry module, from its parsed signatures: Int is bigint, Float number, String string, Bool boolean; List, Option, Result, Pair and Map map to AslList, AslOption, AslResult, AslPair and AslMap, the runtime's own shapes; a schema becomes a readonly interface, an enum a union tagged by variant name, a single capital letter or a declared type variable a generic, (fn [A] -> B) a function type, a type from another module AslOpaque; a name that is not a JS identifier is exported under its ASL name. The prologue declares setOutput, AslTrap, counts and the asl value constructors.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/src/main.asl#compileWithTypes!" :text "compileEntry! plus the TypeScript declarations of the entry module, as (pair js dts).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-js/tests/dtsTest.asl#" :text "Declarations for a typed fixture (schema, enum, generics, Option, a fn parameter, a ?-named export), then, with tsc on PATH: a TypeScript consumer passes tsc --strict and runs against the compiled module with the expected output, and a misuse (a string for a Shape, a JS number for an Int) fails tsc.")
